  "summary": "OpenSSH through 8.7 allows remote attackers, who have a suspicion that a certain combination of username and public key…",
  "details": "OpenSSH through 8.7 allows remote attackers, who have a suspicion that a certain combination of username and public key is known to an SSH server, to test whether this suspicion is correct. This occurs because a challenge is sent only when that combination could be valid for a login session. NOTE: the vendor does not recognize user enumeration as a vulnerability for this product",
